Embedded React: move an opaque page that only a translate moves by copying its pixels.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/animation/animation.c,
engine/scene/compositor.c, engine/scene/er_node_internal.h and
engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt; new file
engine/tests/rendering/test_translate_copy.c.
Not proposed upstream: PS5 React maintains this change here.

A full-screen sheet sliding in by an animated translate repainted its whole box
and what it uncovered on every frame: about 8 million pixels, 10 to 15 ms of
raster per frame at 3840x2160 on eight PS5 cores. An animated translate that is
the only change to its node since the last commit (the new translate_moved
flag) now moves the painted pixels when everything the node paints is one
opaque, plain page inside which its whole subtree lies, seen through no
ancestor that blends or transforms. Like a ScrollView's scroll by copy, it then
repaints only what the move cannot carry: the strips of the page it uncovers,
the area the page left, nodes painted over it, and the moved copies of
footprints vacated inside it. Descendants that changed in the same commit are
repainted by the damage pre-pass at their moved footprints.

